            "creation_time": "2025-09-12T16:05:48Z",
            "count": 1,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "text": "Hoping this is not off-topic.\n\nHere are a couple of hunspell issues.\n\n`https://github.com/hunspell/hunspell/issues/662`\n\n\"aspell handles this: by allowing the user to specify\"\n\n\"might have been contributed but never acted upon\"\n\n`https://github.com/hunspell/hunspell/issues/300`\n\nFrom Sourceforge with a downloadable patch.\n\n`https://sourceforge.net/p/hunspell/patches/18/`\n\n\"Add command line option to extend the built-in TeX command list.\"\n\n\n\"implementation against 1.2.8\"",
            "bug_id": 18944
          },
          {
            "id": 102498,
            "time": "2025-12-22T19:40:20Z",
            "is_private": false,
            "attachment_id": {},
            "tags": [],
            "bug_id": 18944,
            "text": "Sorry for the late reply.\naspell() already has a 'filter' argument which allows specifying a filter *pipeline*, so I would prefer not adding a new argument for more filters.\nI guess the preparsing filter could simply be made into a regular filter?",
            "count": 2,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "creation_time": "2025-12-22T19:40:20Z",
            "creator": "Kurt.Hornik"
          },
          {
            "tags": [],
            "is_private": false,
            "id": 102502,
            "creation_time": "2025-12-23T19:55:47Z",
            "count": 3,
            "bug_id": 18944,
            "text": "\nHoping again not to be off-topic.\n\nSee the aspell entry in info for a comparison to other spell checker engines.\n\n> https://sourceforge.net/p/hunspell/patches/18/\n\nAs regards the above link's patch would the R community have interest in reaching out to the Hunspell developers?",
            "attachment_id": {},
            "time": "2025-12-23T19:55:47Z",
            "creator": "lindblad",
            "is_markdown": true
          },
          {
            "id": 102538,
            "is_private": false,
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Personally, I think it would be nice if hunspell gained better support for (La)TeX preprocessing, but then even what Aspell offers is by far not good enough (no support for user defined environments or verb(atim) things).\nSo afaic the best would be having a fully customizable (La)TeX filter which can be used for all spell checkers, perhaps even written in R.\nFor now, the best we have is the filter based on the LaTeX parsing code in either tools or the {parseLatex} package ...",
            "bug_id": 18944,
            "count": 4,
            "creation_time": "2025-12-31T13:43:11Z",
            "time": "2025-12-31T13:43:11Z",
            "attachment_id": {},
            "is_markdown": true,
            "creator": "Kurt.Hornik"
          },
          {
            "attachment_id": {},
            "time": "2026-06-26T17:11:28Z",
            "creator": "gabembecker",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "tags": [],
            "id": 103241,
            "is_private": false,
            "creation_time": "2026-06-26T17:11:28Z",
            "bug_id": 18944,
            "text": "Hi Kurt,\n\nComing back to this, the reason we proposed a pre-processing filter is that the filter (pipeline, as you pointed out) occurs *after* parsing, which is where the failure is occuring, so a filter won't be able to fix the issue.",
            "count": 5
          },
          {
            "creator": "Kurt.Hornik",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "attachment_id": {},
            "time": "2026-07-01T07:52:20Z",
            "creation_time": "2026-07-01T07:52:20Z",
            "count": 6,
            "text": "Oh dear ... apparently I last worked on the new LaTeX aspell filter 2 years ago.\n\nClearly, currently one cannot compose filters.  So to \"enhance\" an\navailable filter for pre or maybe also post processing one needs to\ncreate a new filter wrapping around the available one, which is not\nsuper-convenient as the available one are not directly accessible.  \n\nThat could be changed by exporting utils:::aspell_filter_db, which I\nguess I should do in any case.\n\nCurrently,\n\nR> names(utils:::aspell_filter_db)\n[1] \"LaTeX\"        \"Sweave+LaTeX\" \"md\"           \"Sweave\"       \"Rd\"          \n[6] \"R\"            \"dcf\"          \"pot\"     \n\nwhere the first two are undocumented (and the second has a \"Try to merge\ninto the Sweave filter.\" FIXME).  The unfortunately-still-undocumented\nLaTeX filter wraps around utils:::aspell_filter_LaTeX_worker() which has\n\nR> args(utils:::aspell_filter_LaTeX_worker)\nfunction (x, cmds = NULL, envs = NULL, parser = tools::parseLatex, \n    ...) \n\nwhich I should document and say that one can also use the\nparseLatex::parseLatex parser, which iirc these days handles errors\n(more) gracefully.  (Need to re-run my test codes and discuss results\nwith Duncan.)\n\nOne could add a 'before' argument to the LaTeX filter/worker, and use as\nsomething like\n\n  if(is.function(before))\n    x <- before(x)\n\nbefore calling the parser on x.\n\nGood enough ...?",
            "bug_id": 18944,
            "tags": [],
            "is_private": false,
            "id": 103267
          },
          {
            "attachment_id": {},
            "tags": [],
